{"type":"system","subtype":"init","apiKeySource":"login","cwd":"/Users/user/work/delegate-12-budgets","session_id":"23269ead-5209-4ac9-9976-6eab6d468682","model":"Composer 2.5","permissionMode":"default"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review follow-up for tests/budgets.rs (only that file). Make one new commit, do not amend, do not push.\n\n1. Watch and models budgets: give them a 50ms floor:\n   `const WATCH_BUDGET_MS: u128 = 50; // measured: 2ms on M-series Mac; 50ms floor, since 3x a spawn-dominated time flakes on CI`\n   Do the same for MODELS.\n2. RSS test: wait until the fake agent has written its pid file (as the cancel test in tests/cli_e2e.rs waits for `agent.pid`) before sampling. Include the measured KB in the assertion message, and also `eprintln!(\"supervisor rss: {kb}KB\")`.\n3. Cancel test cleanup: kill the grandchild `sleep` process, if the fake spawns one, so nothing leaks.\n4. Merge `Env::new_info` into `Env::new(name, script)`. If a table-driven loop over (args, stdin, budget) replaces the six wall-clock tests in fewer lines while keeping each failure message naming the command, do it. Otherwise keep the six tests.\n5. Gates: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --test budgets` 3 times. Report the line count before and after.\n\nCommit message ends `Co-Authored-By: Composer 2.5 <noreply@cursor.com>`. Report the SHA, the line counts and the gate results, then Friction (up to 3 bullets) and a STATUS line.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"23269ead-5209-4ac9-9976-6eab6d468682"}
